# Copy to ~/.config/knowrag/ingest.env and fill in. systemd EnvironmentFile + the
# scheduled-ingest.sh wrapper read this. No secrets belong in the unit files.
#
# Paths are install-specific. The repository keeps only this example.

KNOWRAG_ENV=/absolute/path/to/go-knowrag/.env.knowrag
KNOWRAG_DOTENV=/absolute/path/to/go-knowrag/.env
KNOWRAG_BIN=/absolute/path/to/go-knowrag/bin/cli
KNOWRAG_ENSURE=/absolute/path/to/go-knowrag/scripts/embedder-service/ensure-embedder.sh
# Checkout root — applied_state.json is resolved from the working directory.
KNOWRAG_WORKDIR=/absolute/path/to/go-knowrag

# Optional. The scheduled ingest prunes with --yes, and refuses to prune more than the smaller of this many
# notes and this percentage of a vault's indexed notes in one run (defaults 20 and 5, never below 3 notes).
# Raise them only if the vault really changes size that much between two runs.
# KNOWRAG_PRUNE_MAX_NOTES=20
# KNOWRAG_PRUNE_MAX_PERCENT=5
# Where the last-ingested vault roots are recorded (default $XDG_STATE_HOME/knowrag, ~/.local/state/knowrag).
# KNOWRAG_STATE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/state

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the KNOWRAG_ENV file (.env.knowrag) holds for the owner's vault, which is indexed ONLY under
# its `wiki/` folder (`raw/` has a derived page in `wiki/` for every note, so indexing both would give
# two answers to one question). There is no "include only" setting: `wiki` is the one area, and every
# other first-level folder of the vault is excluded by name. Values below are placeholders.
#
#   KNOWRAG_VAULTS=<name>
#   KNOWRAG_VAULT_<NAME>_PATH=<root of the owner's vault>
#   KNOWRAG_VAULT_<NAME>_AREAS=wiki
#   KNOWRAG_VAULT_<NAME>_EXCLUDE_FOLDERS=raw,<every other first-level folder, comma separated>
#   KNOWRAG_VAULT_<NAME>_EXCLUDE_ROOT_FILES=<the loose .md files at the vault root, comma separated>
#   DEFAULT_COLLECTION=interno_eg2
#
# Folders whose name starts with a dot (.git, .obsidian) are skipped without being listed. A first-level
# folder that is neither the area nor in the exclusion list makes the ingestion fail naming it, which is
# on purpose: a new top-level folder in the vault is decided by a person, not indexed by accident.
# The MCP server's MCP_AREAS is then just `wiki`.

